From 8b4def5682969e1a55d1ea340d3ec145598279f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:49:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give the flashcard review a way out, and the lesson's clothes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a phone the review's top row sat under the status bar: the line saying
which card you were on came out from behind the clock, and the cross that
closes the review was somewhere under the battery. There was no way out of
a review at all.

Both overlays — the starred-word cards and the fill-the-blank practice —
now wear the lesson player's own chrome, which is what fixes it: .d-session
with its top row already taking the status bar's inset, the cross and the
green progress bar across the top, and the results in a footer that goes
green or red under one big button. The card is Duolingo's shape, flat with
four pixels of border along the bottom, and it sits in the middle of the
screen rather than hanging off the top. Multiple choice uses the same
option tiles a lesson does, and the blank is a dashed slot rather than an
underline that fell onto the next line.

The translation from the reader's theme to the path's variables moves to
duo/vars.js, since these two screens now need it as much as the path does.
